    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;313;2656,-1344;Inherit;False;132.7999;131.6001;Vertex;1;312;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;216;1152,-2304;Inherit;False;1159.991;628.7109;Billboard
    Node ;7;270;269;267;268;214;217;215;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;314;2656,-1184;Inherit;False;132.7999;131.6001;Offset;1;315;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;215;1184,-2112;Inherit;False;644.2977;383.7836;;;0,0,0,1;The
    Billboard node will rotate vertex data ( position + normal ) to align object's
    axis to current camera.$$This node is a bit different from all others as it injects
    the necessary code into the vertex body and writes directly on the vertex position
    and normal. $$It outputs a value of 0 so it can be connected directly to a vertex
    port ( only if that port is a relative vertex offset ) or it can be used in an
    Add node so further vertex operations can be placed.$$$Billboards can be set
    through its Type either as Cylindrical where only the object X and Z axis are
    aligned with the camera ( useful when rendering trees ) or as Spherical where
    all axis are aligned.$$Also, through the Ignore Rotation parameter an object's
    initial rotation can be either completely ignored and overridden, or it can be
    used as a delta rotation over the billboard final calculations.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;217;1184,-2240;Inherit;False;214.5789;105.9795;NOTE:
    ;;0,0,0,1;Billboard node should only be connected to vertex ports;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;268;2032,-2240;Inherit;False;210.3335;105.6838;Cylindrical;;0,0,0,1;Only
    aligns object x and Z axis with camera;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;269;2032,-2096;Inherit;False;202.3335;110.6838;Spherical;;0,0,0,1;Only
    aligns object x and Z axis with camera;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;270;1856,-1968;Inherit;False;387;188;Ignore
    Rotation;;0,0,0,1;If turned off, the object initial rotation will be used as
    a delta rotation on top of the billboard final calculated rotation.$$On the other
    way, if turned on the object initial rotation will be completely ignored and
    the final rotation will be only be set by the billboard result.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.BillboardNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;267;1856,-2096;Inherit;False;Spherical;False;True;0;1;FLOAT3;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.BillboardNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;214;1856,-2240;Inherit;False;Cylindrical;False;True;0;1;FLOAT3;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
